<title>JAPAN: Kobe Steel says raises China-bound steel price.</title>
<headline>Kobe Steel says raises China-bound steel price.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-06-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Kobe Steel Ltd said on Thursday that China National Metals &amp; Minerals Import &amp; Export Corp has accepted a price increase for Kobe's steel products to be shipped from August to January.</p>
<p>Kobe said it had increased the price of its hot- and cold-rolled sheets, steel rods, galvanised steel sheets and thick steel sheets for delivery to China by approximately five percent.</p>
<p>Kobe has agreed to ship about 10,000 tonnes of steel a month to China during the August-to-January period, little changed from the preceding six months, a Kobe spokesman said.</p>
</text>
